usage: nascheck [-hqV] [-c config] command [device ...]

commands:
  scan               list the devices reported by smartctl
  status [device]    table of all or the given disks
  check [device]     report problems; exit 0 ok, 1 warning,
                     2 critical, 3 unknown

  -c config  configuration file (default /usr/local/etc/nascheck.conf)
  -q         check: print the summary line only
exit 64
